; A price directive may be followed by a comment and nothing else, as
; the amount of a posting may (#3353).  Ledger used to stop reading a P
; line at the end of its price and drop the rest unread.  The first line
; below, with its price written in single quotes, priced EUR in a
; commodity named '$, because a bare symbol may contain an apostrophe,
; and the closing quote was lost.  The other lines lost the text after
; their prices too, except the lot annotation, which was read as part of
; the price and corrupted the price history.  A price written as an
; expression ends at its closing parenthesis, so only a comment may
; follow that either.

P 2024/01/01 EUR '$1.10'
P 2024/01/02 EUR $1.20 junk
P 2024/01/03 EUR 1.30 USD!
P 2024/01/04 EUR $1.40 @ $2.00
P 2024/01/05 EUR $1.50 {$2.00}
P 2024/01/06 EUR ($1.00 + $0.60) junk
P 2024/01/07 EUR ($1.00) * 1.70
P EUR $1.80 junk
apply fixed EUR $1.90 junk

test pricedb -> 9
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$FILE", line 12:
Error: Unexpected text ''' after the price
While parsing file "$FILE", line 13:
Error: Unexpected text 'junk' after the price
While parsing file "$FILE", line 14:
Error: Unexpected text '!' after the price
While parsing file "$FILE", line 15:
Error: Unexpected text '@ $2.00' after the price
While parsing file "$FILE", line 16:
Error: Unexpected text '{$2.00}' after the price
While parsing file "$FILE", line 17:
Error: Unexpected text 'junk' after the price
While parsing file "$FILE", line 18:
Error: Unexpected text '* 1.70' after the price
While parsing file "$FILE", line 19:
Error: Unexpected text 'junk' after the price
While parsing file "$FILE", line 20:
Error: Unexpected text 'junk' after the price
end test
